From e2d1c5e7ddecbdab89405db90b5aa3432282831f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@localhost>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 00:14:50 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] ANDROID: selinux: keep netlink_xperm off (android16-6.12
 parity)

7.x enforces the netlink_xperm policy capability when the loaded policy declares
it, so NETLINK_ROUTE messages are checked per nlmsg type as ioctl-style xperms.
The Android 17 vendor policy declares the capability but was written for 6.12,
which never enforced it: /vendor/bin/nicmd RTM_GETLINK/RTM_NEWLINK was denied
(phone test 43: avc nlmsg denials, rmnet_data links vanish, 4G data
OEM_DCFAILCAUSE_4). Force POLICYDB_CAP_NETLINK_XPERM to 0 after loading the
policy capabilities, like 6.12 behaves.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 security/selinux/ss/services.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/security/selinux/ss/services.c b/security/selinux/ss/services.c
index 3e3ba78b1..4f01608af 100644
--- a/security/selinux/ss/services.c
+++ b/security/selinux/ss/services.c
@@ -2182,6 +2182,16 @@ static void security_load_policycaps(struct selinux_policy *policy)
 		WRITE_ONCE(selinux_state.policycap[i],
 			ebitmap_get_bit(&p->policycaps, i));
 
+	/*
+	 * ANDROID AVR: 6.12 parity. The Android 17 policy declares netlink_xperm, which
+	 * android16-6.12 does not know (so it kept plain nlmsg_read/nlmsg_write checks);
+	 * the Alor vendor policy was written for that and has no per-message nlmsg xperm
+	 * rules. Enforcing it on 7.3 denies e.g. vendor_nicmd RTM_GETLINK (phone test 43:
+	 * avc denied { nlmsg } nl-msgtype=18 -> sendto -EACCES -> rmnet_data torn down ->
+	 * no 4G data / VoLTE). Keep the 6.12 semantics.
+	 */
+	WRITE_ONCE(selinux_state.policycap[POLICYDB_CAP_NETLINK_XPERM], 0);
+
 	for (i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(selinux_policycap_names); i++)
 		pr_info("SELinux:  policy capability %s=%d\n",
 			selinux_policycap_names[i],
-- 
2.56.1

